                  {
                    "value": "Management Insight\r\nThe priority-informed scenario changes allocation relative to population alone because it also incorporates age-structure vulnerability, census uncertainty and relative mapped facility-location scarcity. Northeast False Creek shows the largest positive illustrative budget shift (+$160,656.11), while Sunset also receives a larger modeled share and remains highly ranked across weighting scenarios. These shifts identify communities for further planning investigation; they do not establish actual funding need or recommended VCH allocations.\r\nScenario totals reconcile exactly to $10M, 50 FTE and 1,000 community-care units.",
